1
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,920
Leyang Huanmeng Park

2
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:06,800
Are you tired?

3
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:07,520
No.

4
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:09,770
Look at the pigeons.

5
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:10,960
So many pigeons.

6
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:11,720
Yeah.

7
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:13,050
Do you want to feed them?

8
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:18,079
You must be thirsty. Have some water later.

9
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:20,440
Dad,

10
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,320
is Mom not coming today?

11
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,600
Mom has been busy.

12
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,060
Dad will spend the day with you today.

13
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:30,320
Are you not having fun today?

14
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,400
I am.

15
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,200
Dad will take you to eat some delicious cake later,

16
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:35,840
okay?

17
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,560
Okay.

18
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,320
My car.

19
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,280
Stop, my car.

20
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,560
Nuannuan, come.

21
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,120
Zhao Jia, what are you doing?

22
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,200
What am I doing?

23
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:54,760
Nuannuan, let's go.

24
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:55,920
You're going too far, Zhao Jia.

25
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:56,560
Who's going too far?

26
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,320
You're the one who took the child away without a word.

27
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,120
Nuannuan, come with Dad.

28
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:00,520
You're hurting her. Let go.

29
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,640
Let go. Nuannuan.

30
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,000
You're hurting her.

31
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:04,640
She's crying. She's crying.

32
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:06,920
Come on, get in the car.

33
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,000
Don't cry.

34
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,280
Why are you being so unreasonable?

35
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,120
I'm being unreasonable?

36
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,000
Give her back to me.

37
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,120
I carried her for ten months and risked my life to give birth to her.

38
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,480
What right do you have to take her?

39
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:19,040
I raised Nuannuan since she was little.

40
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,200
Have you ever cared for her?

41
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,480
Where were you when she needed her mom?

42
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:22,480
I was working.

43
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:23,760
I was making money for this family,

44
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:24,760
working my life away for this family.

45
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:26,040
Without me, could you drive a car like that

46
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,200
or live in a nice house like that?

47
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,880
With your little bit of money, could she go to a private school,

48
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:29,680
Zhao Jia? Could she study abroad?

49
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:30,520
Do you still think Nuannuan and I

50
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,780
need that kind of life?

51
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,520
My income

52
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,960
can also give Nuannuan a life like that.

53
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,240
You're the one who wants too much.

54
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,240
I want too much?

55
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,520
Why didn't you refuse when I gave it to you?

56
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,040
That's why I've had enough of you.

57
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,960
Do you know how suffocating you are?

58
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:41,840
I really hate your

59
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,760
condescending attitude, you know?

60
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,079
Fine.

61
00:03:44,079 --> 00:03:46,940
I'm telling you, you're not taking the child today.

62
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,480
Then let me tell you again.

63
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:49,640
From this moment on,

64
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,200
Nuannuan will not leave my side.

65
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,130
Don't even think about taking her.

66
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:54,320
You're crazy.

67
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:55,920
Do you deserve to be a mother?

68
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,520
Did you forget Nuannuan got hurt because of you?

69
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,680
Nuannuan got hurt because of me?

70
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,520
Do I deserve to be a mother?

71
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,520
What, are you playing the good father now?

72
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,840
If it weren't for you wanting a divorce for your mistress,

73
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:05,360
if it weren't for you abandoning this family,

74
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:07,080
would this family have fallen apart?

75
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,680
Zhao Jia, are you crazy?

76
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:11,410
How am I being unreasonable in front of Nuannuan?

77
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,800
Nuannuan! Nuannuan!

78
00:04:16,959 --> 00:04:19,839
Nuannuan! Nuannuan! Nuannuan!

79
00:04:20,839 --> 00:04:21,680
Nuannuan!

80
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:23,200
Nuannuan!

81
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,040
Nuannuan!

82
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,120
Cheng Fei.

83
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:29,320
How is it?

84
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,610
I'm looking for her.

85
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,240
Here.

86
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:38,840
There.

87
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,040
Here.

88
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,920
It's all your fault. Are you crazy?

89
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:51,120
Why did you make the decision on your own?

90
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:51,800
There are so many cars here.

91
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:52,640
What if she gets hurt?

92
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,800
Would Nuannuan have run away if you hadn't gone crazy?

93
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,680
Who went crazy first?

94
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:55,480
Who acted shamelessly first?

95
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,240
Because of you. Enough.

96
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:56,960
It's because of you.

97
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:57,840
Enough.

98
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,800
Stop it, both of you.

99
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:05,330
The most important thing now is to find Nuannuan.

100
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:07,480
Do we have cameras from other angles?

101
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,040
These are the only ones at the park entrance.

102
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,900
We didn't capture anything else.

103
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,320
Let's split up and search.

104
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:13,960
Split up.

105
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,080
Did you see a little girl?

106
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,440
Did a student from our school come back?

107
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,120
Xixi's mom.

108
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:23,840
Nuannuan's mom. Xixi.

109
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,120
Did Nuannuan look for you today?

110
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,280
Have you seen this child?

111
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:26,720
No.

112
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,460
Then I'll leave you my number.

113
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,220
She took classes here.

114
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,440
She has pigtails.

115
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,159
No.

116
00:05:32,159 --> 00:05:33,220
I haven't seen her.

117
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:52,000
Can we come out and play often in the future?

118
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,040
Xiaolong, I found Nuannuan.

119
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,100
She's at the campsite from last time.

120
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:20,920
Nuannuan.

121
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,920
Nuannuan, why are you here?

122
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,680
Uncle.

123
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,280
I don't want to go home.

124
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:36,930
That's perfect.

125
00:06:39,159 --> 00:06:40,820
I don't want to go home either.

126
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:50,159
The little bird's parents.

127
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,370
Will they get a divorce too?

128
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:58,600
Is it because of me

129
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:01,120
that they fight so much?

130
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,360
If I were cut in half,

131
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,880
one half for each of them,

132
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:09,280
would they stop fighting?

133
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:14,440
Nuannuan.

134
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,650
Mom and Dad fighting is their problem.

135
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,650
It's not your fault.

136
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,320
But I don't want them to get a divorce.

137
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,540
I don't want to.

138
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,620
Actually, parents getting divorced

139
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:39,480
isn't as scary as you imagine.

140
00:07:50,159 --> 00:07:51,920
When I was your age,

141
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:57,920
my parents also got divorced.

142
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:01,560
I was also very scared back then.

143
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,280
But later I realized

144
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,740
it wasn't what I expected.

145
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,840
They treated me

146
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,160
even better than before.

147
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:16,800
They never argued again.

148
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,960
They spoke gently

149
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,380
and joked with each other.

150
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:25,480
On my birthday,

151
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,730
they would pick me up together,

152
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,520
buy me gifts,

153
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,760
and take me out for good food.

154
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:36,799
When I was sick,

155
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:39,360
they would take care of me

156
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,080
and stay with me.

157
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,060
Great. Take another step.

158
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,520
Will they still take you out to play?

159
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:56,400
Yes.

160
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,320
We went to many places together.

161
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:02,220
We went to the amusement park,

162
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:03,600
the zoo,

163
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,880
and went hiking and swimming together.

164
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,570
What about when you grow up?

165
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,480
Is it the same?

166
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,240
When you grow up, you'll find

167
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:20,760
that many things will pass.

168
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:27,000
The good, the bad,

169
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,760
the happy, and the unhappy,

170
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,580
they will all pass.

171
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:37,480
We will be fine.

172
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,610
Even if we are alone,

173
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:43,720
we will be fine.

174
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,000
Will we really?

175
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:51,440
Yes.

176
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,680
Finding Nuannuan that day

177
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,000
was all thanks to you.

178
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,480
Thank you.

179
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:38,680
Cheng Fei.

180
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,040
Let's talk.

181
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,880
As your attorney,

182
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:54,040
I really should have argued strongly with Xiaolong.

183
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:57,040
But later I realized

184
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,240
we both have a common client,

185
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,290
who is Nuannuan.

186
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,130
Her interests are the most important.

187
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:10,240
Jiajia.

188
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:13,000
The trial is tomorrow.

189
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,400
Should we

190
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,280
reconsider

191
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:20,680
whether to keep fighting for custody?

192
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:28,400
I know.

193
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,160
Nuannuan is very important to you.

194
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:36,160
But she has already run away from home once,

195
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:38,420
which means she's in a lot of pain.

196
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:40,240
When the trial starts tomorrow,

197
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,120
forcing her

198
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:43,360
to choose between you and her father

199
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:47,520
is just too cruel.

200
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:52,320
Nuannuan is my own flesh and blood.

201
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:58,240
If one of us

202
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,720
has to

203
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,960
get hurt,

204
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,120
it definitely has to be me.

205
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,240
It must be me.

206
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:06,560
So...

207
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,360
What's wrong?

208
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:18,840
Cheng Fei said

209
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:22,160
he's giving up custody of Nuannuan.

210
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:22,920
He wants to

211
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:25,640
handle the divorce with me peacefully.

212
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,200
Although a divorce decree ends

213
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,730
the marital relationship,

214
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,280
it does not sever

215
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,530
the relationship between parents and children.

216
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,600
You and Zhao Jia will always be

217
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:47,960
Nuannuan's parents.

218
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,200
As she grows up,

219
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:52,480
you play an indispensable role.

220
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:57,080
Please don't leave

221
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:59,610
invisible scars in the child's heart.

222
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,080
You're here.

223
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:46,400
Xiaolong.

224
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,200
Dad.

225
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,850
There's something I want to talk to you about.

226
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,040
My son is home.

227
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:59,280
Look, I timed it perfectly.

228
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,640
Hurry up and wash your hands for dinner.

229
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:04,380
That's enough.

230
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:07,120
Thank you, son.

231
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:11,360
Have a taste.

232
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:14,440
These are all your favorite dishes from childhood.

233
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:16,480
See if they still taste the same.

234
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,170
Thanks, Mom.

235
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:22,600
How is it?

236
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:24,960
Delicious.

237
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:26,540
Have some more.

238
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:31,800
Son.

239
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:33,440
Well,

240
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,560
I've thought it through.

241
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:37,400
As for Li Guochen's signature,

242
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,860
if he won't sign, let it be.

243
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,400
Don't put yourself in a tough spot.

244
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,640
I'll handle it myself.

245
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:43,570
It just means waiting a bit longer.

246
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:45,770
Actually, Dad called me today.

247
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:49,240
He asked when I'd be free to take you

248
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,760
to sign the paperwork with him.

249
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:09,760
Where are you going? I'll give you a ride.

250
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:10,520
No need.

251
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,040
I don't need it.

252
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,720
We're not going the same way.

253
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:18,010
I'm leaving.

254
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,900
Li Guochen is getting old too.

255
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,400
No dispute over property.

256
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,040
Child custody goes to the mother.

257
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:48,720
The father has visitation rights.

258
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,920
Any questions?

259
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:51,400
No problem.

260
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:57,360
Number 7092, please go to window 23.

261
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:57,890
June 6th.

262
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:03,640
Number 7093, please go to window 23.

263
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:09,920
Number 7093, please go to window 23.

264
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:34,000
Where are you going?

265
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:34,680
To work.

266
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,240
And you?

267
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:37,160
Same.

268
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:46,560
Zhao Jia.

269
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:49,120
I sincerely hope

270
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:52,560
you will have a good life.

271
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:57,400
Me too.

272
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,440
From now on,

273
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:03,640
we should both have a new beginning.

274
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:07,720
See you this weekend.

275
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:08,920
See you this weekend.

276
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:32,280
Here I come. Careful.

277
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,240
Be careful.

278
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:36,400
Little Nuannuan, the eagle is coming.

279
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,640
Careful.

280
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,040
Got you! Got you!

281
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,760
Then I'll be the eagle this time.

282
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:44,420
You be the hen and protect Mom.

283
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:47,760
Okay.

284
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:48,920
Get behind me.

285
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,280
Are you ready?

286
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,640
Ready.

287
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,360
This is so nice.

288
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,160
Xiaolong.

289
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,400
You can't catch me.

290
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,480
Thank you.

291
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,440
Just cry if you want to.

292
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:39,240
It's no big deal.

293
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,000
Look.

294
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,120
Even the popsicle is crying.

295
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:07,520
Come on.

296
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:17,600
If you get any inside information in the future...

297
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:18,840
Just tell me.

298
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,000
I know it's hard to get into that group.

299
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,400
Can you put in a good word for me with the group leader?

300
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,680
Given our relationship.

301
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,740
Don't you trust me?

302
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:26,760
Right.

303
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,560
I'll treat you to a meal some other day.

304
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:29,120
Okay.

305
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:33,960
So rude.

306
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:46,680
Huzi.

307
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:51,200
Dali.

308
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:57,560
Why are you back?

309
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:00,800
How many years has it been since we last saw each other?

310
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:01,640
Ten years.

311
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:02,320
Exactly.

312
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,160
Let's have a good drink.

313
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,760
It's on me. We won't leave until we're drunk.

314
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:05,240
Okay.

315
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,570
Let's have some drinks.

316
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:08,880
Give me that one.

317
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:11,890
Let's have that one, the most stylish one.

318
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,160
Great.

319
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:14,660
Of course it is.

320
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,360
Are you sure, bro?

321
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,640
This bottle is 3,500.

322
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:21,010
What do you mean?

323
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:23,080
Are you looking down on us?

324
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,320
I'm just reminding you.

325
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,280
It's fine.

326
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:25,780
Open it.

327
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:26,720
Don't open this one.

328
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:27,960
I have money.

329
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:28,400
It's fine.

330
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:30,000
Change it to the most expensive one.

331
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:30,640
Okay.

332
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,160
No, Dali.

333
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,000
We don't need to do this.

334
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:36,560
Boss.

335
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:38,820
This bottle is 18,000.

336
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:39,960
18,000?

337
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:42,520
Is it the most expensive one?

338
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,480
I thought this place was high-end.

339
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:47,080
Open it.

340
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,120
Don't open it.

341
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:48,520
You...

342
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,240
This bottle of wine will cost me my family's bathhouse.

343
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:50,720
Dali, you don't have to.

344
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,520
Swipe the card.

345
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:53,250
How could I let you spend money?

346
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:56,960
What's going on with you?

347
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,760
How come you're so rich now?

348
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:00,760
Did you get that money legally?

349
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:01,320
Let me tell you.

350
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:02,840
I'm running a law firm with a friend now.

351
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:05,170
If you have any problems, you must tell me.

352
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:07,520
Don't worry.

353
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:11,360
My dad gave me this money.

354
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,120
Did your mom get married again?

355
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:16,380
What second marriage?

356
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:20,000
My mom got cancer a few years after moving away.

357
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,560
She borrowed from loan sharks but couldn't be cured, and passed away.

358
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:25,360
Later, I became a loan shark too.

359
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:27,940
You... well, aren't you still...

360
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,200
That's all in the past.

361
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,160
I quit a long time ago.

362
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,240
Don't worry.

363
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:34,240
Then what did you mean by 'dad'?

364
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:37,640
Growing up,

365
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:39,280
my mom always told me my dad was dead.

366
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,480
I told you about this.

367
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,130
I never believed it.

368
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:44,000
I always felt he was still alive.

369
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:47,320
A while ago, an old man came looking for me.

370
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,920
He said he's my biological father

371
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,580
and wanted to acknowledge me.

372
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:52,920
I... I never thought I was...

373
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,240
I'm a rich kid.

374
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,940
Tell me, isn't my dad impressive?

375
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,320
You watch too much TV.

376
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:02,040
Are you the youngest son of a chaebol?

377
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:03,280
A rich kid?

378
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:08,720
Dali, you...

379
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:11,300
Are you telling the truth?

380
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:11,680
When I did

381
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:12,800
the DNA test,

382
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:14,200
I was so nervous.

383
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:16,320
I was afraid it wasn't true.

384
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:19,120
Yeah.

385
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:22,880
I, Dali, am completely back this time.

386
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,680
You're doing great now.

387
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,440
Gel in your hair,

388
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:27,960
and this little chain is really nice.

389
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:28,680
Hermès.

390
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:29,520
What about this?

391
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,380
Constantin...

392
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,080
Vacheron.

393
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:31,770
Zombies?

394
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:33,920
Huzi,

395
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,480
let's get rich together.

396
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:36,720
Getting rich sounds good.

397
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,280
Right?

398
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,280
Cheers.

399
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,440
Beautiful lady,

400
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,300
did you leave the door open for me?

401
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:56,020
Does your back hurt again?

402
00:22:56,040 --> 00:22:57,720
Don't keep using these patches if your back hurts.

403
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:59,680
Why don't we go to the hospital and get it checked?

404
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,360
What? It's an old problem.

405
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:02,520
Why waste money on that?

406
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:04,240
But I have money.

407
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,240
The law firm pays me a salary,

408
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:07,890
and I also trade stocks.

409
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,480
Come on, with the little money you have,

410
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:10,640
you should save it

411
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,680
to get a wife first.

412
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:16,400
What are you doing?

413
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:19,000
Where did you go drinking? You reek of alcohol.

414
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:20,240
You know who,

415
00:23:21,120 --> 00:23:21,600
Dali.

416
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:22,720
Who?

417
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:23,880
Dali.

418
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:27,080
Hasn't he been out of town for years?

419
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:27,720
Yeah.

420
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:31,520
Didn't he live with his mom since he was a kid?

421
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:34,780
Then his biological father suddenly showed up.

422
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,480
And his biological father

423
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:38,120
is a super rich

424
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:38,760
big boss.

425
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:40,280
What?

426
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:42,200
Now,

427
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:44,240
I have every reason to suspect

428
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:46,360
that my father

429
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:49,680
might also be a hidden...

430
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:51,080
You had a few drinks

431
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:52,940
and now you're talking nonsense.

432
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:56,160
Give me that hot water bottle,

433
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:57,560
and go to sleep.

434
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:58,280
Got it.

435
00:23:58,920 --> 00:23:59,600
You don't need to hold it.

436
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:00,080
Give it to me.

437
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:00,920
You're not feeling well. Let me do it.

438
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:01,800
I'll do it myself.

439
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:02,920
Come on. Is it here?

440
00:24:04,120 --> 00:24:04,800
Here?

441
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:06,480
A little lower.

442
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:08,480
Okay, okay. Don't touch it. It's hot.

443
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,960
A little higher.

444
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:19,920
I'm telling you, with me here,

445
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:21,200
our law firm is bound to win.

446
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,480
We'll definitely win the championship.

447
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:23,920
Cows are flying in the sky,

448
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:25,160
because Brother Hu is blowing hot air on the ground.

449
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,480
What am I bragging about?

450
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:29,240
When I was a kid, I was known as the Badminton King of Heping District.

451
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:30,080
Really?

452
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:31,840
I almost made it to the district team when I was a kid.

453
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:33,520
You didn't even make the district team?

454
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:34,960
Okay, I know your level now.

455
00:24:34,960 --> 00:24:37,360
He's equivalent to my hometown township's

456
00:24:37,360 --> 00:24:37,960
middle-lower level.

457
00:24:37,960 --> 00:24:39,360
My district is huge.

458
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:39,920
Lower-middle.

459
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:41,050
What lower-middle?

460
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:42,680
You're quite agile.

461
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,360
Longnv.

462
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:45,480
Class monitor.

463
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:46,560
I'm number 24.

464
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:47,520
What number are you guys?

465
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,440
We are

466
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:49,200
on the 7th.

467
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:50,920
Who are you playing against on the 7th?

468
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:51,680
Who is it?

469
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:12,200
Since your back is bad,

470
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:13,520
we'll give you a three-point head start,

471
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:14,880
so you can't say we're bullying you.

472
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:16,120
Can you stop showing off?

473
00:25:16,120 --> 00:25:17,560
We don't need your head start.

474
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:18,920
Mr. Li, let's give them ten points,

475
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:20,120
so they don't lose too badly.

476
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:21,840
It's fine. It's good that someone is giving away points.

477
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:23,040
Just don't regret it.

478
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:26,000
Both players, get ready.

479
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:33,040
Nice shot!

480
00:25:34,280 --> 00:25:35,140
Come on, Uncle!

481
00:25:38,040 --> 00:25:39,120
Beautiful!

482
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:40,600
Awesome!

483
00:25:41,560 --> 00:25:42,890
There you go. Good shot.

484
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,040
Good shot!

485
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:03,440
Good shot, Lawyer Li.

486
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:08,320
Nice!

487
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:18,960
Uncle.

488
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:20,810
Where is your Feather King?

489
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:22,120
No, no, wait a minute.

490
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:23,320
Why are you guys so excited?

491
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:24,280
Referee, you saw it, right?

492
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:25,920
I gave them a three-point head start at the beginning.

493
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:26,640
This is against the rules.

494
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:28,480
You guys played well.

495
00:26:28,840 --> 00:26:29,320
You played well.

496
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:31,440
I gave you a three-point head start at the beginning, didn't I?

497
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:33,400
Don't make a fool of yourself.

498
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,680
No, it was just...

499
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:35,840
Accept your defeat.

500
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:37,880
You insisted on giving them a handicap.

501
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:38,480
No, I...

502
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:40,640
Drink some water.

503
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:42,880
I am the Badminton King.

504
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:44,040
Are you the Badminton King?

505
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:45,000
I am the Badminton King.

506
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,930
I am the King of Kings in badminton.

507
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,240
Let's get the car.

508
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:55,600
We'll use our car to hit his car.

509
00:26:55,600 --> 00:26:57,400
Go hit your brother Beihu's car.

510
00:26:58,920 --> 00:26:59,680
Does it look like a big tiger?

511
00:26:59,680 --> 00:27:00,360
Lao Tian.

512
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:02,280
Stop playing and call everyone to eat.

513
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:02,760
Sister-in-law.

514
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:03,800
Thank you, sister-in-law.

515
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:04,800
Why don't you take a rest?

516
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:05,520
Stop, stop cooking.

517
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:06,520
Just one last dish of fried pork slices left.

518
00:27:06,520 --> 00:27:07,040
Coming right up.

519
00:27:07,040 --> 00:27:08,640
Don't stop your sister-in-law.

520
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:10,400
She hasn't made this dish in a long time.

521
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:12,280
If it weren't for you guys, I wouldn't get to eat it.

522
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:13,920
Who told you to have high blood pressure, blood sugar, and cholesterol?

523
00:27:13,920 --> 00:27:15,080
You can only have one bite later.

524
00:27:15,080 --> 00:27:15,720
I'm telling you.

525
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:17,280
Don't worry, Sister-in-law. We'll keep an eye on him.

526
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,040
If you ask me,

527
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:19,680
Old Class Monitor, you really need to take care of your health.

528
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:20,680
Stop staying up late.

529
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:22,040
Don't work yourself to death.

530
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:22,880
Our bodies now

531
00:27:22,880 --> 00:27:24,600
aren't like they were in college, right?

532
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:25,040
Right.

533
00:27:25,040 --> 00:27:26,720
I feel like back when I was taking the bar exam,

534
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:28,600
I stayed up night after night.

535
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:30,360
Did she tell you guys?

536
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:32,200
Her bar exam story is so annoying.

537
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,860
She passed it on her first try.

538
00:27:34,320 --> 00:27:35,960
It's not worth mentioning.

539
00:27:36,040 --> 00:27:37,000
It's all luck.

540
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:38,760
Excellent since childhood.

541
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:40,400
You guys probably don't know.

542
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:42,720
The old monitor got a really high score on the bar exam.

543
00:27:42,720 --> 00:27:43,920
You should ask him for advice.

544
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:46,040
I took it three times.

545
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:49,040
By the end, even the questions recognized me.

546
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:51,600
Old monitor, you took it that many times too?

547
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,200
I've taken it five times now,

548
00:27:53,440 --> 00:27:54,360
but I still haven't passed.

549
00:27:54,360 --> 00:27:55,720
Is this something to be proud of?

550
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:56,920
Why are you telling everyone?

551
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:58,800
Three or five times is nothing.

552
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:01,280
People like us just get braver with every setback.

553
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:01,920
To sum up,

554
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:04,760
I just slowly grew up

555
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:06,280
through setbacks and failures.

556
00:28:06,280 --> 00:28:07,120
Later on, I even...

557
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:09,400
I even wrote a bar exam guidebook myself.

558
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:10,000
Wanna see?

559
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:13,250
Fried pork slices are here!

560
00:28:13,480 --> 00:28:14,240
Come on.

561
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:15,080
Come on, eat up.

562
00:28:15,080 --> 00:28:16,560
I don't know if it suits your taste.

563
00:28:16,560 --> 00:28:18,040
It's perfect.

564
00:28:18,800 --> 00:28:20,730
You two are perfect for each other.

565
00:28:21,040 --> 00:28:23,120
You have to return it to me.

566
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:24,520
Luo Zhi, let me tell you.

567
00:28:24,520 --> 00:28:26,520
This isn't just a bar exam guidebook.

568
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:28,280
It's my old monitor's blood, sweat, and tears.

569
00:28:28,280 --> 00:28:29,920
It's my life.

570
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Look at his white hair.

571
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,040
It's from staying up late back then.

572
00:28:32,040 --> 00:28:33,600
Come on, let's eat.

573
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:36,610
You have guests.

574
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:39,200
Grandma Feng.

575
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:40,480
Is Lawyer Tian here?

576
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:41,560
Old Tian.

577
00:28:42,040 --> 00:28:42,720
Lawyer Tian.

578
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:43,080
Grandma.

579
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:45,280
Xiaoxue has locked herself

580
00:28:45,440 --> 00:28:47,560
in her room for a long time.

581
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:50,560
I'm worried something might have happened to her.

582
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:51,960
Did anyone answer when you knocked?

583
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,290
No, Xiaoxue can't hear.

584
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:54,560
Let's go take a look.

585
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:54,960
Hurry.

586
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:55,720
Go.

587
00:29:04,640 --> 00:29:05,240
Be careful.

588
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:05,800
Child.

589
00:29:08,760 --> 00:29:09,520
Xiaoxue.

590
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:10,760
Save her. Hurry.

591
00:29:10,760 --> 00:29:11,120
Hurry.

592
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:12,400
I'll make a call. Get the car.

593
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:13,040
Lift her up.

594
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:13,760
Slow down.

595
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:14,920
Hold her legs. Legs.

596
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:16,040
No, I didn't get a good grip.

597
00:29:16,040 --> 00:29:17,520
Okay. Let's go. Slowly.

598
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:19,000
Grandma.

599
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:19,840
Don't worry.

600
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:33,920
Doctor, how is the child?

601
00:29:33,920 --> 00:29:35,320
She took an overdose of sleeping pills.

602
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:37,280
After gastric lavage, she is temporarily out of danger.

603
00:29:37,280 --> 00:29:39,040
But you still need to keep a close eye on her.

604
00:29:39,040 --> 00:29:39,600
Grandma.

605
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:41,320
It's good that she's fine.

606
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:43,920
Why do you think Xiaoxue suddenly took things so hard?

607
00:29:43,920 --> 00:29:45,200
Did something happen?

608
00:29:45,520 --> 00:29:46,560
I don't know.

609
00:29:48,080 --> 00:29:49,000
What happened?

610
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:50,560
Grandma.

611
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:51,920
Xiaodong.

612
00:29:51,920 --> 00:29:52,780
How is Xiaoxue?

613
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:55,740
The doctor said she's just out of danger.

614
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:56,720
It's all my fault.

615
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:58,580
I shouldn't have argued with her.

616
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:01,320
Why did you argue?

617
00:30:01,320 --> 00:30:03,380
I lost my temper and broke up with her.

618
00:30:03,400 --> 00:30:06,600
But I really didn't expect her to do something so foolish.

619
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:07,520
It's all my fault.

620
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:08,000
Child.

621
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:09,600
Don't be like this.

622
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:11,320
How could this be your fault?

623
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:12,720
The patient just woke up.

624
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:13,650
Please be quiet.

625
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,280
You're awake.

626
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:28,040
Xiaoxue.

627
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:29,760
It's me, Weidong.

628
00:30:30,760 --> 00:30:31,520
I was wrong.

629
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,200
Let's not break up,

630
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:33,920
okay?

631
00:30:33,920 --> 00:30:35,120
I'll never mention breaking up again.

632
00:30:35,120 --> 00:30:35,920
Don't move around.

633
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:36,920
You're on an IV.

634
00:30:36,920 --> 00:30:37,920
I know, I know.

635
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:39,400
You're just mad at me, right?

636
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:40,560
We'll never be apart again.

637
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:42,160
All right, save it for tomorrow.

638
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:42,960
Let the patient get some rest first.

639
00:30:42,960 --> 00:30:43,720
Okay.

640
00:30:43,720 --> 00:30:44,600
I'm sorry.

641
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:46,020
This is my girlfriend.

642
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:47,800
We had a fight.

643
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:49,040
And she just...

644
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:56,240
Did Feng Xue really try to kill herself over a breakup?

645
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:58,320
Why do I feel like something's off?

646
00:30:58,520 --> 00:31:00,120
From what her grandmother said,

647
00:31:00,120 --> 00:31:02,040
they definitely had a conflict.

648
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:05,920
Don't you guys think Feng Xue is really afraid of him

649
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:07,520
and strongly resisting him?

650
00:31:07,560 --> 00:31:08,840
The director is right.

651
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:10,920
What Feng Xue just said was,

652
00:31:11,960 --> 00:31:13,820
"Go away. I don't want to see you."

653
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:15,760
How do you know?

654
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:17,280
I know sign language.

655
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:19,280
You know sign language?

656
00:31:19,760 --> 00:31:21,020
That's a hidden skill.

657
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:22,280
When did you learn it?

658
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:24,080
I've known it since I was a kid.

659
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:25,840
Since you were a kid?

660
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:28,040
That's a pretty unique skill to have.

661
00:31:28,520 --> 00:31:30,560
My parents are deaf.

662
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:35,040
It's fine.

663
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,920
Actually, they're no different from hearing people.

664
00:31:39,760 --> 00:31:42,440
They are very willing to communicate with others,

665
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:43,840
hope to be understood,

666
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:45,840
and are willing to understand others.

667
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:48,170
Some deaf people even learn lip-reading.

668
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:50,600
But that Wei Dong just now,

669
00:31:51,040 --> 00:31:53,080
he was just talking to himself,

670
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:55,720
completely ignoring the fact that Feng Xue couldn't hear.

671
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:57,600
Right, it didn't seem like a conversation.

672
00:31:57,600 --> 00:32:00,040
It was like he was just talking to himself.

673
00:32:00,040 --> 00:32:00,840
Director,

674
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:02,520
I don't think Feng Xue

675
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,600
tried to commit suicide over a relationship.

676
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:06,040
I have the same feeling.

677
00:32:06,560 --> 00:32:08,760
But why does it seem like her grandmother

678
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,960
